This project is an independent, clean-room implementation produced for
interoperability: it lets OpenPort 2.0 hardware keep working with standard
SAE J2534 applications on current versions of Windows, where the original
vendor driver no longer installs.

"Tactrix" and "OpenPort" are trademarks of their respective owner. This project
is NOT affiliated with, authorized by, or endorsed by that owner. Those names
are used only nominatively, to state which hardware this software is compatible
with.

No vendor code or vendor binaries are included in this repository. The wire
protocol documented here was determined by observing the device's own USB CDC
interface and by lawful reverse-engineering for interoperability (see, e.g.,
EU Directive 2009/24/EC Art. 6 and 17 U.S.C. §1201(f)). The SAE J2534 API
definitions are an industry interface specification, not proprietary to any
single vendor.

